            "html": "<p>Nothing in the arithmetic is contradictory. A has a relatively young population, so a large fraction of its residents belong to the group where deaths are less common. B has a relatively old population, so more of its people belong to the group where deaths are more common. B's two subgroup rates are lower, but its age distribution pulls the overall rate upward. The crude total blends <em>what happens within age groups</em> with <em>how many people live in each age group</em>.</p>"
