            "html": "<p>This kind of aggregate-versus-subgroup reversal is associated with <strong>Simpson's paradox</strong>. The general issue of aggregation and association was discussed by scholars before Edward Simpson's 1951 paper; Simpson was not the inventor of age standardization, nor did Graunt and Halley formulate the modern paradox. The connection here is <strong>conceptual</strong>, not a claim of direct transmission.</p>"
