    "references": "<ol><li><strong> John Graunt (1662)</strong>, <em>Natural and Political Observations… Made upon the Bills of Mortality</em>. <a href=\"https://wellcomecollection.org/works/ear22f7e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wellcome Collection, first edition</a> — digitized original; <strong>Public Domain Mark</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong> Appleby &amp; Stahl-Timmins (2018)</strong>, <a href=\"https://www.bmj.com/content/363/bmj.k5014\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Consumption, flux, and dropsy: counting deaths in 17th century London</em></a>, <em>BMJ</em>. Historical treatment of the mortality bills and Graunt's comparisons.</li>\n<li><strong> Connor (2024)</strong>, <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10919065/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>John Graunt F.R.S. (1620–74)</em></a>. Historical context and the limits of the surviving records.</li>\n<li><strong> Portrait caution</strong>, <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7670870/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Is This a Portrait of John Graunt?</em></a>. No authenticated portrait is known.</li>\n<li><strong> Edmond Halley (1693)</strong>, <a href=\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/101946\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>An Estimate of the Degrees of the Mortality of Mankind…</em></a>, <em>Philosophical Transactions</em>. Original source for the Breslau life table.</li>\n<li><strong> Bellhouse (2011)</strong>, <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/jrsssa/article-abstract/174/3/823/7077758\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>A New Look at Halley's Life Table</em></a>. An assessment of the historical table and its assumptions.</li>\n<li><strong> Historical data</strong>, <a href=\"https://search.r-project.org/CRAN/refmans/HistData/html/HalleyLifeTable.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Halley's Life Table</em></a> and <a href=\"https://search.r-project.org/CRAN/refmans/HistData/html/Breslau.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Breslau records</em></a>. For historical context, not a claim of modern reliability.</li>\n<li><strong> Norton (2015)</strong>, <a href=\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1740-9713.2015.00844.x/full\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Simpson's paradox … and how to avoid it</em></a>, on Yule, Simpson, and the history of aggregation reversals.</li>\n<li><strong> CDC/NCHS</strong>, <a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/hus/sources-definitions/age-adjustment.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Age adjustment</em></a>. Direct standardization formula and interpretive caution.</li>\n<li><strong> United Nations</strong>, <a href=\"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/Standards-and-Methods/files/Handbooks/crvs/Series_F7-E.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Handbook of Vital Statistics Methods</em></a>. Crude rates, standardization, and interpretive issues.</li>\n<li><strong> WHO</strong>, <a href=\"https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/gho-documents/global-health-estimates/gpe_discussion_paper_series_paper31_2001_age_standardization_rates.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Age Standardization of Rates: A new WHO Standard</em></a>. Weighting and the dependence on standard choice.</li>\n<li><strong> William Farr portrait</strong>, <a href=\"https://wellcomecollection.org/works/kmc5cvzu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wellcome Collection catalogue</a>. This particular reproduction is catalogued <strong>in copyright</strong>; this particular reproduction is not used here.</li></ol>"
